window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Sold to the Morozov Bratva.</b></p> <p>I convinced myself I could survive 365 days as his captive wife. Get my bookstore back. Simple, right?</p> <p>Wrong.</p> <p>I wasn't ready for the raw, vajayjay-clenching desire in his look. The way he devours me night after night. He promises to ruin me for any other man. And I'm paying for my naivety,</p> <p>One filthy groan at a time.</p> <p>I also didn't foresee the hunger. The vomiting. The three positive pregnancy tests.</p> <p>Victor Morozov's baby.</p> <p>Growing inside me.</p> <p>Just as I think it's happily ever after, Eli and I get kidnapped. To save us, Victor must die... But I won't let that happen.</p> <p>Not to the father of my child. Not to the man I've grown to... Love?</p> <p>Velvet Chains <i>wraps up the Bond by Morozov Bratva duet. Catch up with Victor and Laura from book one,</i> Silken Chains <i>as they head towards a super satisfying happily ever after.</i></p>"; 
